msgctxt "#30031"
msgid "Save the stream manifest"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30032"
msgid "Writes the DASH manifest of the next stream you play into the addon's profile folder as last-manifest.mpd, for diagnosing playback failures."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30010"
msgid "Playback"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30011"
msgid "Maximum resolution"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30012"
msgid "Caps the video height InputStream Adaptive will select. Useful on hardware that cannot decode 1080p smoothly."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30013"
msgid "Unlimited"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30014"
msgid "1080p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30015"
msgid "720p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30016"
msgid "480p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30020"
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30021"
msgid "Client version"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30022"
msgid "The YouTube TV web player version this addon claims to be. Google bumps it regularly; a stale value is the likeliest cause of sudden sign-in failures."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30023"
msgid "Licence proxy port"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30024"
msgid "Local port for the Widevine licence proxy. Change it only if something else on this machine already uses it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30025"
msgid "Visitor ID (set automatically)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30026"
msgid "Proof-of-origin token"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30027"
msgid "Google requires a proof-of-origin token on media requests. Without one the CDN refuses every segment. Tokens are tied to a browser session and expire after a few hours."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30033"
msgid "Compare YouTube TV client identities"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30034"
msgid "Before playing, asks every YouTube TV client (web, Android, iOS, TV) for the same video and logs what each is offered. Used to find a client served plain URLs rather than SABR."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30037"
msgid "JavaScript runtime"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30038"
msgid "Full path to node, deno, bun or quickjs. Needed to compute the n parameter every media URL carries; without it playback is refused. Leave empty to search PATH and the usual locations. Set it explicitly when Kodi is a flatpak or on LibreELEC, where the runtime lives somewhere Kodi does not look."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30035"
msgid "Resume where you left off"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30036"
msgid "Start a title at the position YouTube has for this account, the same one the web player resumes from. It comes back with the stream, so nothing is stored on this machine. Live channels always start at the live edge."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30039"
msgid "Report progress to YouTube"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30040"
msgid "Send the playing position to YouTube while a title plays, so it counts as watched and resumes here and on every other device. Turn this off to watch without it reaching your account."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30045"
msgid "Integration"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30046"
msgid "Install IPTV Manager add-on"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30047"
msgid "Enable IPTV Manager integration"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30048"
msgid "Publish the YouTube TV channel list and guide to IPTV Manager, so the channels appear in Kodi's own TV section with a full EPG instead of only inside this add-on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30049"
msgid "IPTV Manager settings…"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30050"
msgid "IPTV Manager channels endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30051"
msgid "IPTV Manager EPG endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30052"
msgid "Account"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30053"
msgid "Google API client ID"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30054"
msgid "Only needed for the experimental \"Sign in with a code\" option. This is your own Google API project, the same client ID and secret the YouTube add-on asks for; none is shipped with this add-on. Signing in from your phone or laptop needs neither."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30055"
msgid "Google API client secret"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30056"
msgid "Check whether SABR could replace the cookie sign-in"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30057"
msgid "Asks three things and writes the answers to the log: whether the Widevine licence server accepts the credential you are signed in with, whether this session is offered a SABR endpoint, and whether that endpoint serves a request once the n parameter is solved. Plays nothing and changes nothing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30058"
msgid "Play through SABR when signed in with a code"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30059"
msgid "The cookie jar is used for playback whenever there is one, because it is offered a DASH manifest and plays through the ordinary path. Turn this on to use a code sign-in instead when you hold both: that identity is only ever offered SABR, so playback goes through the bridge. One quality per track unless the adaptive setting below is on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30060"
msgid "Always play through the SABR bridge"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30061"
msgid "Ignore the DASH manifest even when one is offered, so a cookie session plays through the bridge too. This exists to tell two things apart that are otherwise always changed together: the credential and the delivery. The same recording, byte for byte the same media, decrypts on the DASH path and does not through the bridge -- so if it also fails here on cookies, the bridge is at fault, and if it plays, the token's licence is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30062"
msgid "Paste this together with the proof-of-origin token, from the same browser capture. A session-bound token is bound to the visitorData that minted it: the addon bootstraps its own visitorData from the page it loads with your cookies, which is a different session from your browser's, so a token minted there can never satisfy urls bound to this one. Same account, different session identity, and the media is refused with an empty-bodied 403."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30063"
msgid "SABR endpoint override"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30064"
msgid "Diagnostic. A url pasted here is used instead of the one the player response carries, exactly as pasted. Paste one a browser was served and this answers whether the urls we are issued are refused or our client is: the same url that returned megabytes to the browser either works here or it does not. Leave empty for normal playback."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30065"
msgid "Cold start the proof-of-origin token"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30066"
msgid "Nothing in this addon needs a JavaScript runtime any more: n is solved by the bundled Python interpreter, and the proof-of-origin token is minted by running BotGuard's own interpreter inside a JavaScript engine written in Python. Turn this on to skip the mint and compute a token arithmetically instead -- it costs nothing and works while YouTube reports StreamProtectionStatus 2, but it is good for thirty minutes rather than twelve hours. It also stops n falling back to a runtime if one happens to be installed, so this is the switch for seeing exactly what a box with Python and nothing else does."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30067"
msgid "Let the player choose the quality on the bridge"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30068"
msgid "The bridge names one rendition per track, because SABR chooses server-side: fields 16 and 17 of a request are the set the client can play and the server picks out of it. Turn this on and the manifest lists every H.264 rendition instead, and whichever one InputStream Adaptive asks for is the only one still offered on the next exchange. Off by default: a narrowed set was once refused outright, and if it is refused again the session goes back to the whole set for the rest of playback. On a protected title a rendition is only listed once its key id can be named -- read out of its own media, or out of a licence this title has already been granted -- because a Representation whose PSSH names no key is a manifest InputStream Adaptive refuses whole."
msgstr ""
